# Raging-Potato
Taking my journey from Cybersecurity student to Cybersecurity professional through continuous learning, projects and practical experience.

## About me

Hi, I'm Ash. 
This blog will document my journey from Cybersecurity student to Cybersecurity professional. This space I've created, will track my learning, share projects, document labs and reflect on lessons learned along the way.

## My Professional Background

I currently work as a Senior Access Control Technician, where I design, install, maintain and service electronic security systems. My role has given me hands-on experience with physical security, along with some exposure to the IT world and the ability to troubleshoot complex issues in real-world environments.

Working in the security industry has sparked my interest in Cybersecurity, especially as more products and services rely on online infrastructure. We are becomming increasingly dependent on digital technologies for communication, social media, banking, entertainment, and many other aspects of everyday life.

This realisation got me thinking: as our reliance on technology continues to grow, the need for Cybersecurity will grow with it. Protecting systems, networks, and data will become more important than ever. So why not start learning about it now and build the skills needed for the future?

This blog is a record of that journey-from Senior Access Control Technician to aspiring Cybersecurity professional.

## Current Focus

I am currently building my foundational knowledge in cybersecurity and information technology. Coming from a physical security background, I am investing time in understanding networking, operating systems, cybersecurity principles, and the tools commonly used in the industry. 

I am also gaining hands-on experience through labs, practical exercises and personal projects to develop technical skills that complement my existing security industry experience.

### Short Term Goals

- Strengthen my understanding of networking and IT fundementals.
- Gain practical experience through labs and projects.
- Build a portfolio that demonstrates my learning and progress.
- Continue developing the skills required for entry-level cybersecurity roles.

### Long Term Goals

- Transition into a cybersecurity-focused career.
- Earn industry recognised certifications.
- Contribute to protecting organisations from cyber threats.
- Continue growing and learning as a cybersecurity professional.

## Final Thoughts

Starting something new can be challenging, especially when stepping from a predominantly physical security environment into the digital world. Cybersecurity is broad and constantly evolving. While I'm still at the beginning of my journey, I'm comitted to developing the skills, gaining the certifications, and completing the projects needed to achieve my goals and build a future in cybersecurity.

This blog, will serve as a record of my progress, experiences, successes and setbacks as I work towards building a new career in cybersecurity. My hope is by sharing my journey, I can not only track my own growth but also connect with others who are following the same path.

Thanks for taking the time to visit, and I look forward to seeing where this journey leads.

